Use Rust as main programming language.

The rust game engine project is based on the ECS system and custom memory allocation. The ECS architecture currently consists of the following modules: core (entity, archetype, component, ecs master). And this one, memory (memory allocation, memory pools containing chunks, which, in turn, store components of a certain type. And the structure of the chunk itself).

At the moment, only the ECS system is being developed. 

The project minimizes overhead runtime and uses approaches for maximum performance and cache locality. The ECS system should support further lock-free concurrency integration. The project does not use hashmap, dyn, mutex and other slow mechanisms. The project can use low-level unsafe optimizations

